    "reason": "[ev-508cd6635da3] says that when a cluster-scoped resource wrongly has metadata.namespace set, the repo-server may apply the wrong tracking annotation. The fix has the app controller run a follow-up normalization that corrects that annotation. Nothing in the evidence says anything fails, is rejected or must be migrated. After the upgrade, the controller just writes a different (correct) tracking annotation on these malformed resources, so behavior-change (review) fits [ev-9fdf3ef2828b]. The evidence does not set the severity; medium is a judgement call, so confidence is low.",
